{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-dq-squared-elaboration-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:dq-squared-elaboration-intro","kind":"prose","text":"dq-squared-elaboration-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:dq-squared-elaboration-intro\"></a><p>We specialise the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2</code> obstruction and the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Lie bracket Jacobiator to a concrete manifold <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M</code>. At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>, all deformed operators recover their classical counterparts.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared-elaboration-intro.md","heading":""}
